.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Animate a collection of targets with one script clock\&. 

\fBTroupe\fP inherits \fBAnimated\fP's controls and exposes the same semantic subclass commands as \fBAnimationScript\fP\&. \fBadd()\fP, \fBremove()\fP and \fBclear()\fP edit direct membership\&. Sprites, Parts, \fBAnimatedAttributes\fP, ordinary \fBAnimated\fP targets and other Troupes are accepted\&. Members are borrowed; keep their native objects or JavaScript wrappers alive while using them\&. Expired targets are skipped\&. Self-membership and cycles throw\&. A repeated direct add is idempotent\&. Nested membership is flattened in insertion order and a leaf target receives each operation once, even when multiple membership paths reach it\&.

.PP
Commands use each member's own coordinate system and activation-time baseline\&. A batch or series has collective completion dependencies, and a conditional or until evaluator for the shared graph sees the \fBTroupe\fP\&. Staggering an entire block creates separate member executions; evaluators inside that staggered block see the member target\&. Targets and order are captured when the block is published\&. Removing a member stops its outstanding contribution on the next \fBTroupe\fP update; additions participate in subsequently published blocks\&.

.PP
Advance the \fBTroupe\fP with animate(deltaSeconds) once per frame, before its members' ordinary animation updates when using programmed-rate profiles\&. The \fBTroupe\fP drives only its shared script; it does not call \fBSprite\fP physics, drawing, managers or nested Troupes' independently scheduled work\&. Members retain their normal update owners\&. Member setters interrupt matching \fBTroupe\fP channels\&. Programmed-rate contributions are integrated by the \fBTroupe\fP and consumed once by the member's next ordinary update\&. \fBTroupe\fP snapshots serialize direct members, including nested Troupes, through object references and preserve collective playback and saved marks\&. A restored \fBTroupe\fP retains its loaded members\&. \fBPart\fP members reference the owning \fBSprite\fP and stable \fBPart\fP ID, so a separately saved \fBSprite\fP or layer shares the same restored \fBPart\fP\&. Detached Parts have no standalone snapshot format and raise an error\&. Write layers, Troupes and independently saved members through the same \fBSerializer\fP to share identities without duplication\&. Full layer records use object references for Sprites\&. Layers do not automatically include Troupes; the application must explicitly save each \fBTroupe\fP whose collective animation should resume\&. Saving a member alone preserves its own animations, while collective playback is stored in the \fBTroupe\fP\&. 
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
const dancers = new pdg\&.Troupe()\&.add(alice)\&.add(bob);
dancers\&.moveBy(50, 0, 1)\&.stagger(0\&.1)\&.andThen()\&.rotateBy(1, 0\&.5);

.fi
.PP
 
.RE
.PP
